    {
      "id": "far-bt-journal-and-trial-balance-c1",
      "heading": "The case and what is asked",
      "explanation_md": "**Bharat Gupta** starts **Bharat Traders**, a proprietary firm trading in **Product X**, on 1 April 2006. He hires an office in Delhi at **Rs. 2,500 per month**. The slide lists **21 transactions** for April with the date, transaction number and amount.\n\nThe question asks you to show the **voucher for the first transaction** and to **record all the transactions in the journal**. The handwritten note adds that you must then prepare: **1) a trial balance, 2) a profit and loss account, 3) a balance sheet.**\n\nPlan: write each transaction as a debit and a credit, keep running balances for each account, then list the balances.",
      "example_ids": [
        "far-ex-bharat-case"
      ],
