    {
      "id": "far-bt-journal-and-trial-balance-c2",
      "heading": "Journal entries 1 to 10",
      "explanation_md": "| No. | Debit | Credit | Amount (Rs.) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cash | Capital (Bharat Gupta) | 1,50,000 |\n| 2 | Bank (State Bank of India current account) | Cash | 1,35,000 |\n| 3 | Rent | Bank | 2,500 |\n| 4 | Scooter | Regent Automobiles | 31,500 |\n| 5 | Regent Automobiles | Bank | 7,500 |\n| 6 | Furniture | Cash | 8,500 |\n| 7 | Equipment | Bank | 11,500 |\n| 8 | Purchases | Bank | 45,000 |\n| 9 | Bank | Sales | 12,500 |\n| 10 | Advertisement | Bank | 2,200 |\n\n**Notes.** Transaction 2 moves money from cash into a bank account. Transaction 4 is a credit purchase of the scooter (the vendor bears all initial costs including insurance). In transaction 5 the down payment of 7,500 reduces what is owed to Regent Automobiles; the remaining **24,000** (31,500 less 7,500) is a loan payable in 12 monthly instalments from May 1 with interest at 12% a year on the reducing balance. Interest starts after April, so none is recorded for April.",
      "example_ids": [
        "far-ex-bharat-scooter"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Scooter 31,500 on credit, 7,500 down payment, balance 24,000 is a loan with 12 monthly instalments at 12%.",
