    {
      "id": "far-bt-journal-and-trial-balance-c3",
      "heading": "Journal entries 11 to 21",
      "explanation_md": "| No. | Debit | Credit | Amount (Rs.) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | Purchases | ABC & Co. | 75,750 |\n| 12 | RIL & Co. | Sales | 31,875 |\n| 13 | Cash | Sales | 6,425 |\n| 14 | Bank | RIL & Co. | 31,875 |\n| 15 | ABC & Co. | Bank | 75,750 |\n| 16 | Purchases | ABC & Co. | 30,450 |\n| 17 | RIL & Co. | Sales | 25,600 |\n| 18 | Salary | Cash | 3,500 |\n| 19 | Drawings (Bharat Gupta) | Bank | 4,000 |\n| 20 | Telephone | Cash | 650 |\n| 21 | Petrol | Cash | 550 |\n\n**Notes.** Entries 11, 12, 16 and 17 are on credit (15 days for ABC & Co., one week for RIL & Co.). Entries 14 and 15 settle them by cheque. Entry 19 is a cheque to the owner for personal use, so it is **drawings**, not an expense. Entries 18, 20 and 21 are expenses paid in cash (the salary of the office assistant Sudaamaa, the telephone and the petrol for the scooter).",
