    {
      "id": "far-bt-journal-and-trial-balance-c4",
      "heading": "The trial balance of Bharat Traders",
      "explanation_md": "After posting every entry to its account and balancing, the balances are:\n\n| Account | Debit (Rs.) | Credit (Rs.) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cash | 8,225 | |\n| Bank | 30,925 | |\n| RIL & Co. | 25,600 | |\n| Scooter | 31,500 | |\n| Furniture | 8,500 | |\n| Equipment | 11,500 | |\n| Purchases | 1,51,200 | |\n| Rent | 2,500 | |\n| Advertisement | 2,200 | |\n| Salary | 3,500 | |\n| Telephone | 650 | |\n| Petrol | 550 | |\n| Drawings | 4,000 | |\n| Capital | | 1,50,000 |\n| Sales | | 76,400 |\n| ABC & Co. | | 30,450 |\n| Regent Automobiles (loan) | | 24,000 |\n| **Total** | **2,80,850** | **2,80,850** |\n\nHow the key balances arise: Cash = 1,50,000 - 1,35,000 - 8,500 + 6,425 - 3,500 - 650 - 550 = 8,225. Purchases = 45,000 + 75,750 + 30,450 = 1,51,200. Sales = 12,500 + 31,875 + 6,425 + 25,600 = 76,400. RIL & Co. owes 31,875 + 25,600 less the 31,875 received, so 25,600. ABC & Co.: 75,750 + 30,450 less 75,750 paid, so 30,450. Both columns total 2,80,850.",
